sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-daphnia-magna-turing-wavelength-s0> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-daphnia-magna-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-daphnia-magna-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Daphnia magna ocellus-pigment Turing wavelength at 2.736 µm (Holocene, detail scale) — MorphoEval overall 86.4/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 2 of the Holocene Daphnia magna detail-tier model. Analytical λ_c remains 2.736 µm at 0 Ma on a chronoseries of length 1. The full scored band still has Pearson r = 0.99999995 (RMSE 0.000125). The odd indexed modes, withheld from the fitting narrative, have Pearson r = 0.99999978 (RMSE 0.000123). The saturated peak is 3.7212 µm, a coarsening ratio of 1.3601 against a no-shift reference of 1. The D_u sweep still lengthens λ_c by 2.21, and equal diffusion still decays (ratio 0.286). The cuticle mesh peak stays at 20.17 µm. Outline circularity 0.018 is the antennule and carapace folds; aspect ratio 1.43 is the shape number. The GIF is 12 frames at 720×540 and its last frame is the CC BY-SA SEM. Signing is still blocked: there is no nanopub profile. Overall 86.4/100 (faithfulness 85.1, reproducibility 89.3); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 5b213d4525d0e9f71d5fc4e385d270b87ac07ec8; environment: python 3.12, numpy 1.26.4, note scipy 1.18 and Pillow 13 installed for this run; no virtualenv. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 90, Morphological realism / specimen match 76, Parameter expressivity 88, Morphometric validation 92, Source and data traceability 92, Code-to-model traceability 88, Reproducibility package 88. Output judged: docs/media/daphnia_magna_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-daphnia-magna-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 5b213d4525d0e9f71d5fc4e385d270b87ac07ec8, image/png, 345784 B, 1512×960 px, artifact_sha256 9fac22d3c08e135df897db24e03d94c054b312d965f2f92d026ad6f6765b31f1 (sha256 9fac22d3c08e135df897db24e03d94c054b312d965f2f92d026ad6f6765b31f1), spec_fingerprint 5cc7a733d6eb0f2c8ca309d68942c0dd30e27b59c80a745c4958e462d76f9c31. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 5cc7a733d6eb0f2c8ca309d68942c0dd30e27b59c80a745c4958e462d76f9c31; artifact_sha256: 9fac22d3c08e135df897db24e03d94c054b312d965f2f92d026ad6f6765b31f1. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-27-daphnia-magna-turing-wavelength-s0-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing (1952) selects λ_c = 2π/k_c. Schnakenberg (1979) supplies du/dt = a − u + u²v and dv/dt = b − u²v. | Macagno (1981), Smith & Macagno (1990), and Hebert & Emery (1990) are the Daphnia sources for visual-system pattern formation, ommatidial photoreceptors, and inducible cuticular melanin. None of them reports a 2.736 µm stripe period.; reconstructed_in_script: Length unit fixed so the analytical wavelength is 2.736 µm, with a = 0.062, b = 1.180, D_u = 0.016, D_v = 0.640. | Pass 2 scores σ(k) on the odd modes of the band σ > -0.15 separately from the full band. Both exceed r = 0.98. | The ratio of the saturated Fourier peak to 2.736 µm is reported as coarsening, not as a second target wavelength.; transfer_boundary: Age does not change along this 1/1 chronoseries. The melanosome and ommatidium comparisons are scale comparisons. | The 20.17 µm cuticle peak does not transfer to the 2.736 µm field, and the 2.736 µm field does not transfer to the polygons.; does_not_claim: Does not claim a published 2.736 µm measurement. | Does not claim the ×130 polygons are the Turing pattern. | Does not claim a signed nanopublication. ~/.nanopub/profile.yml is absent, and no signature was fabricated. | Does not claim a second independent assessor.." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: {'id': 'R3', 'item': 'Nanopub signing is still blocked. ~/.nanopub/profile.yml does not exist, and no signature was created. Pass 1 items R1 (held-out modes), R2 (coarsening ratio), and R4 (circularity wording) are closed.'}" ;
        pk:hasScore "0.864"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 (builder-assessor, pass 2)" ;
        dct:identifier "grok-4.7" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> .
}

